[00:40.62]Conversation One
[00:42.57]M: Guess what? The worst food I've ever had was in France.
[00:47.63]W: Really? That's odd. 
[00:49.79]I thought the French were all good cooks.
[00:52.98]M: Yes. That's right. 
[00:55.10]I suppose it's really like anywhere else, though. 
[00:58.45]You know, some places are good, some bad. 
[01:02.03]But it's really all our own thought.
[01:04.60]W: What do you mean?
[01:06.31]M: Well, it was the first time I'd been to France. 
[01:09.96]This was years ago when I was at school. 
[01:12.80]I went there with my parents' friends, from my father's school. 
[01:16.88]They'd hired a coach to take them to Switzerland.
[01:20.10]W: A school trip?
[01:21.62]M: Right. Most of them had never been abroad before. 
[01:25.63]We crossed the English Channel at night, and we set off through France, and breakfast time arrived, and the coach driver had arranged for us to stop at this little caf¨¦. 
[01:36.23]There we all were, tired and hungry, and then we made the great discovery.
[01:42.14]W: What was that?
[01:43.62]M: Bacon and eggs.
[01:45.60]W: Fantastic! The real English breakfast.
[01:49.32]M: Yes. Anyway, we didn't know any better¡ªso we had it, and ugh...!
[01:55.54]W: What was it like? Disgusting?
[01:58.55]M: Oh, it was incredible! 
[02:01.01]They just got a bowl and put some fat in it. 
[02:03.65]And then they put some bacon in the fat, broke an egg over the top and put the whole lot in the oven for about ten minutes.
[02:11.58]W: In the oven! You're joking. 
[02:14.71]You can't cook bacon and eggs in the oven!
[02:17.98]M: Well, they must have done it that way. 
[02:20.84]It was hot, but it wasn't cooked. 
[02:23.78]There was just this egg floating about in gallons of fat and raw bacon.
[02:28.60]W: Did you actually eat it?
[02:30.87]M: No! Nobody did. 
[02:33.27]They all wanted to turn round and go home. 
[02:36.44]You know, back to teabags and fish and chips. 
[02:39.84]You can't blame them really. 
[02:41.54]Anyway, the next night we were all given another foreign speciality.
[02:46.16]W: What was that?
[02:47.98]M: Snails. That really finished them off. Lovely holiday that was!
